  "original_request_utf8": "AGENTWATCH-FOLLOW-UP v1\nsource=src-c946289c8fc1ff74faf4fbc0\nrun=run-685706ba8c60b1e15f47126ff98be675f978cf4d084c31ad4f4e1a70a3821ede\npackage=pkg-27f82cd7-dcb1-4305-a5dd-278495b4c140\nrequest=pixel-idle-20261030-r1\n\n[gap core-poses]\nframes t=306000,315000 every=3000 max=3 edge=1920 ocr=true\nwhy: Recover the one-pixel body shift and the early timeline before later frame counts change.\n\n[gap chest-tone-transition]\nframes t=428000,437000 every=3000 max=3 edge=1920 ocr=true\nwhy: Recover adjacent chest highlight states; OCR cannot establish sub-pixel changes.\n\n[gap arms-delay]\nframes t=622000,631000 every=3000 max=3 edge=1920 ocr=true\nwhy: Recover delayed hand motion at native resolution.\n\n[gap hair-settle]\nframes t=732000,741000 every=3000 max=3 edge=1920 ocr=true\nwhy: Recover the hair flare and settling states, poorly served by sparse stills.\n\n[gap leg-shading]\nframes t=874000,883000 every=3000 max=3 edge=1920 ocr=true\nwhy: Recover lower-body shading detail omitted by the Compact pixel budget.\n\n[gap breathe-reorder]\nframes t=950000,959000 every=3000 max=3 edge=1920 ocr=true\nwhy: Recover tag and frame reordering so early 10-12 frame counts are not mistaken for the final count.\n\nEND-AGENTWATCH-FOLLOW-UP\n",
